 "why_this_exists": [
  "The SECOND edition, and the check on every threshold tuned on the first.",
  "beethoven5-clef-sweep.json is one scanned Beethoven 5, and a threshold fit",
  "to one printer's ink is the failure this area keeps repeating. This is a",
  "different publisher, a different engraver and a different century of",
  "printing, chosen for that reason \u2014 the same reason",
  "ground-truth-mahler5-p72.json was made.",
  "",
  "Method (tools: benchmarks/omr-clef-geometry/sweep_located_clefs.py): run",
  "the locator with clustering ON over pages 4-220 every 4th page, take every",
  "staff it LOCATES a C clef on, render the head of that staff, and read the",
  "glyph by eye. 105 located reads over 1015 header cells on 55 pages. Every",
  "one was read at 2.2x in montages, and the 45 read from a small tile first",
  "were re-read enlarged before being recorded.",
  "",
  "Forty-one of the 105 are not C clefs \u2014 24 treble and 17 bass \u2014 and they are",
  "what a veto change exists to remove. The remaining 64 are genuine C clefs",
  "and are here as the counterweight: a veto that fired on everything would",
  "score perfectly without them.",
  "",
  "WHAT THIS EDITION ADDS THAT BEETHOVEN COULD NOT SHOW. Beethoven's false",
  "positives are all misread CLEFS. Twenty-four of the forty-one here are not",
  "a clef at all: Peters prints the stacked instrument numbers (1/2, 1/2/3) to",
  "the LEFT of the bracket, close enough to the staff to enter the header",
  "window, and a stack of two or three numerals is glyph-sized and vertically",
  "symmetric. That family is invisible in Beethoven and is the single largest",
  "false-positive source here.",
  "",
  "AND IT KILLS THE TENOR FLOOR. On Beethoven the real tenor clefs (0.809 -",
  "0.959) and the tenor misreads (0.702 - 0.795) do not overlap, which looked",
  "like a clean symmetry threshold. Here the real tenor clefs run from 0.708",
  "and the tenor misreads reach 0.845 \u2014 the populations sit on top of each",
  "other. See the write-up in RESULTS.md."
 ],
